          "columns": {
            "teff": "Teff",
            "logg": "logg",
            "u1": "a",
            "u2": "b"
          }
        },
        "qualification": "Photosphere color from a blackbody at the star's published temperature, dimmed toward the limb by the quadratic law Claret & Bloemen (2011), A&A 529, A75 compute from ATLAS model atmospheres for the Johnson V band at 6,319 K and log g 4.19 (u1 0.369, u2 0.307): a model, because no fit of this star's limb is used. The disc is unresolved: no map or absolute brightness is implied. Self-luminous, so no lighting."
      }
